# vocabulary-learning (Magic English) — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
AI-powered vocabulary learning web app (Magic English). Multi-user, Supabase-backed, with AI word analysis and quizzes.
- **Backend**: Node.js + Express.js (`backend/`) — REST API, AI service, Supabase client
- **Frontend**: React + Vite + Tailwind CSS (`frontend/`) — JavaScript only (no TypeScript)
- **Database**: PostgreSQL via Supabase (RLS, auth, realtime)
- **AI**: Multiple providers (Ollama Cloud, OpenAI, local Ollama)
- **CI**: Self-hosted GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) — see `docs/ci-self-hosted-runner.md`
- **Deploy**: Coolify on Hetzner (Docker; project `i8luqt7n49kugwqwfbcyrfvl`) — see `docs/COOLIFY_DEPLOYMENT.md`; merge to `main`/`master` runs CI then `.github/workflows/coolify-deploy.yml`
- **Production:** https://voca.kenchange.com (API `https://voca-api.kenchange.com`)
  - Backend / frontend Dockerfiles under `backend/` and `frontend/`
  - Legacy Railway/Nixpacks files may still exist; Coolify is the production path

## Architecture
```
backend/
  src/
    server.js           # Express entry + middleware
    routes/             # words, users, ai, profile, …
    services/           # AI, Quiz FSRS, enrichment helpers
    middleware/         # auth, errors
    config/             # Supabase
  sql/                  # migrations / functions
frontend/
  src/
    App.jsx             # routing
    pages/              # page components
    components/         # UI (Dashboard, Flashcards, Layout, …)
    contexts/           # Auth, Theme
    lib/                # API client + utils
supabase/               # Supabase-related assets
.github/workflows/      # ci.yml (self-hosted), release.yml
plans/                  # feature plans
docs/                   # setup, CI runner, deploy notes
```

## Key Rules

### Security — CRITICAL
- NEVER log, print, or commit secrets (`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, JWT secrets, AI API keys, OAuth secrets)
- `.env` / `.env.local` are gitignored — verify after every change
- No API keys or secrets in frontend source; frontend may only use public Supabase anon key + URL
- Prefer parameterized queries / Supabase client APIs — never concatenate user input into SQL
- Auth: rely on Supabase session / backend auth middleware for data routes — never assume the caller is authenticated

### Auth paths
- Browser: Supabase Auth (session in frontend `AuthProvider`)
- Backend: validate JWT / user from Supabase for protected routes
- Keep UI gating and API gating in sync — both matter

### AI providers
- AI calls live under `backend/src/services/` — handle timeouts, non-200, empty content
- App features must degrade when AI keys are unset (clear error, no crash)
- Respect rate limits; bulk AI work must not block the event loop unboundedly

### Code Style
- **No TypeScript** — use JavaScript (`.js` / `.jsx`) matching the repo
- Match existing Express + React/Vite + Tailwind patterns
- Prefer small, explicit fixes over broad refactors
- Don't remove broken code — fix it or flag it

### Database / migrations
- Schema changes go through SQL under `backend/sql/` (and/or `supabase/`) with safe guards (`IF NOT EXISTS` where applicable)
- Destructive ops need confirmation / careful defaults — production data lives in Supabase

### Testing / verification
- Smoke: `npm test` (Quiz FSRS) — keep green when touching quiz/schedule logic
- Frontend: `npm run lint` in `frontend/` when ESLint is configured; always verify build with `npm run build`
- Auth changes: signed-in, signed-out, and invalid-token paths
- UI changes: screenshots in the PR description before `[ready]`
- CI: self-hosted runner — see `docs/ci-self-hosted-runner.md`

### Git & Deployment
- PR workflow (worktree-per-PR, babysit until `[ready]`, merge only on ask, deploy verify, worktree cleanup): see `.cursor/rules/pr-workflow.mdc` and `.cursor/skills/ve-pr-workflow/SKILL.md`
- Worktrees live under `../vl-worktrees/pr-<N>`; session title `vl-<PR#>` after PR exists
- Merge into **main** (no squash)
- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `ci:`
- PR hygiene: only related commits — verify `git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD`
- Branch hazard: always verify current branch before git ops
- **PRs — always open / ready for review (never draft)** unless the user explicitly asks for a draft. `ManagePullRequest` `create_pr` must pass `draft: false`. Automation may create a draft — immediately `gh pr ready <N>` and verify `isDraft: false`
- **PR reviews — fix or reply, never ignore:** every review comment/thread (human or bot) must be either fixed in code or answered on GitHub explaining why it is not relevant. Do not mark `[ready]` or merge with unanswered reviews.
- Production: Coolify project id `i8luqt7n49kugwqwfbcyrfvl` — after CI on `main`/`master`, `coolify-deploy.yml` queues backend + frontend
- Do not change Coolify env/secrets as part of routine deploy

### UI Changes
- Preserve the existing Tailwind / app visual language unless the task redesigns it
- Attach screenshots in the PR description before `[ready]` (see `.cursor/skills/ve-pr-workflow/SKILL.md`)
- Verify mobile layout when touching chrome / learning flows

### Severity Calibration
- **Critical (must fix)**: auth bypass, SQL injection, credential exposure, data loss
- **Warning (follow-up)**: missing validation, unsafe defaults, AI error handling, rate-limit gaps
- **Ignore**: formatting diffs, lockfile noise, non-deterministic AI content

## Environment
- Node.js 20+ (see `.nvmrc`)
- Local: `npm run install:deps && npm run dev` (frontend ~3002, backend ~3012)
- Cursor project rules/skills under `.cursor/` are authoritative for agents — do **not** treat root `CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/` kit docs as the source of truth for this repo’s workflow
